  "preamble": "Betacism turns the labiodental [v] into the bilabial stop [b]. In Northern, Central and Northwestern Catalan, /v/ merged into /b/, so viure 'to live' is [ˈbiw.ɾə] while Balearic and Valencian keep [ˈviw.ɾə]. In Eastern and Central Indo-Aryan, Sanskrit and Prakrit v, a labiodental [ʋ] filed here under v, became b in inherited vocabulary: Prakrit vahū 'bride' gave Bengali বউ bou and Hindi बहू bahū. The Castilian Spanish b/v merger is not counted here, because Old Spanish ⟨v⟩ was the bilabial fricative [β], not [v].",
